          "date": "2026-11-03 23:26:37.000000000",
          "tz": -480
        },
        "subject": "LU-21061 lod: put new file objects on directory pool",
        "message": "LU-21061 lod: put new file objects on directory pool\n\nA default LMV that names a pool keeps the subdirectories of a tree\non the MDTs of the pool, but the objects of new files in the tree\nstill go on any OST.\n\nIn lod_ah_init(), give each component of a new regular file that\nnames no pool the pool of the parent's default LMV, if the pool has\nOSTs.  DoM and foreign components are left alone, and a default file\nlayout that names a pool still wins.  The parent's default LMV is\nread only when the MDT has pools.  Files in a subdirectory whose\ndefault LMV is only on the client, such as one that existed before\nits parent got a default, are not limited.\n\nOpen-creates from one process into a directory on MDT0 do not slow\ndown (single VM, 4 MDTs, 3 OSTs, 10000 files, median of 3 runs):\n\n  no pool in the filesystem                6243 creates/s\n  a pool exists, directory names no pool   6254 creates/s\n  directory default LMV names the pool     6330 creates/s\n\nTest-Parameters: mdscount=2 mdtcount=4 testlist=ost-pools\nSigned-off-by: Di Wang <diwa@nvidia.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm\nChange-Id: Ic6413573dd2d5b05e628d32117a253d7697e52fa\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
